tar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov","html_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1915,"digest":"sha256:0b1a690855d28d19be458a49ca7990962aecdfa59b002214a17c314c335953b2","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-23T03:16:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T03:16:48Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/download/v0.90.0/verification.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/tarball/v0.90.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/zipball/v0.90.0","body":"## RevealLine v0.90.0 — Continuous Next across the mission library\n\nThe deliberate **Next** action on a completed mission now continues directly into the next mission in the same mode across campaign, pack, edition, and collection boundaries. It preserves authored order inside each sequence, then follows the unified Journey, Classic, and Custom library order without inserting a picker or summary interruption.\n\nSolo, Versus, and Team preserve their existing mode, party, controller, difficulty, preference, ownership, replay, and progression rules. Cross-host transitions preflight the exact destination picture before leaving the result screen. Missing, ambiguous, unavailable, failed, or cancelled destinations remain visible recoverable outcomes and never record a clear or skip. The final mission does not wrap or switch mode.\n\nSource: `c585bcd3220438da971e2927763b966f55ee8235` (tree `09de27014c17b338fd102e8ac3f300cdd8b88b9f`), merged through [PR #287](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/pull/287).\n\nThe exact-head [PR checks](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/actions/runs/35810431715) passed mandatory preflight and the ordinary production build. The focused source cohort passed 52 checks covering same-sequence order, cross-campaign and collection boundaries, same-name distinct editions, all three modes, the final library end, missing identity, download failure/cancellation, result continuity, finite Versus settings transport, and controller-seat restoration. That cohort is separate from the waived full automated suites.\n\nThe actual merged-source [qualification and freeze](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/actions/runs/35812605127) passed source identity, validation, lint, formatting, native formatting, motion syntax, production reproduction/readiness, and immutable freeze. Automated suites were explicitly waived under the temporary reviewed policy; no passing full-suite verdict is claimed.\n\nThe guarded read-only [artifact inspection](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/actions/runs/35813162247) verified every Git source blob/type/mode and source TAR commit, every distribution manifest byte and hash chain, and the bounded offline inventory. The PR-head-to-merge difference is limited to 64 accepted Pages-controller and v0.89 preservation files; no game, package, lockfile, workflow, or test content changed after the reviewed PR head.\n\nOriginal distribution: 591,122,142 bytes, SHA-256 `9014614f8fe0cb234460d859615b432c098487b21d9e9ae9446b943e35abbb87`.\n\nOriginal source archive: 1,625,630,720 bytes, SHA-256 `0be6bf264577cb385200ff0816189fc8124382cf9352e3310c4525526a6f9872`.\n\nPages selection, predecessor preservation, public byte verification, and bounded browser checks remain separate acceptance gates until the selector PR is merged and the deployed site is checked. A failure after a successful cross-document navigation still uses the receiving host's existing recovery; restoring the previous live result across that failed navigation is not guaranteed. Physical controllers, physical touch, cold-offline use, full campaign balance, and musical/listening acceptance are not claimed by this release package.\n"}